course: dictionary
lesson: 15176
title: Scrunch: squeeze it, crunch it, scrunch it up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scrunch is a word you can see, hear and feel. Look at the words around it to work out which meaning fits. «Ben scrunched the paper into a tight ball and threw it in the bin.» Ben squeezed the paper until it was small and crumpled, so scrunch means to squeeze or crush something into a small, untidy shape.
explain: «Mia scrunched up her nose at the smell of the old fish.» Mia did not squeeze paper here. She made her face tight and crinkled, which shows she did not like the smell. So scrunch can also be about your face or eyes, when you squeeze them tight.
explain: «We heard the scrunch of snow under our boots.» Here scrunch is a noun, a sound. It is the crunching noise you hear when you walk on snow, gravel or dry leaves. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Scrunch is a verb: to scrunch, scrunches, scrunched, scrunching.
fact: Scrunch can also be a noun: a scrunch is the crunching sound of walking on gravel, snow or dry leaves.
fact: «Scrunch» means to squeeze or crush something into a small, untidy ball or shape.
fact: «Scrunch up your face» or «scrunch your eyes» means to squeeze them tight, often because of sun, dislike or worry.
fact: In art, scrunched tissue paper makes good flowers and textures for a collage.
exercise: «Ben scrunched the paper into a tight ball.» What does scrunched mean? | Folded neatly into a square | Torn into long strips | *Squeezed into a small, crumpled shape | Smoothed out flat
exercise: «We heard the scrunch of snow under our boots.» What is a scrunch in this sentence? | A pair of warm boots | A cold wind blowing hard | *The crunching sound of walking on snow | A snowball thrown at a friend
exercise: «Mia scrunched up her nose at the smell.» What does this action show? | Surprise at a present | Happiness | *Dislike | Tiredness
test: «Ellie scrunched her eyes shut against the bright sun.» What did Ellie do? | Opened her eyes wide | Winked at her friend | *Squeezed her eyes tight | Rubbed her eyes with a towel
test: In a science test, which material would you most likely scrunch into a ball? | Wooden block | *Tissue paper | Glass window | Steel rod
exam: Which phrase means to squeeze your face tight? | Scrunch the leaves | Scrunch of gravel | Scrunched-up paper | *Scrunch up your face
